# UI/UX and Component Guidelines

## Design Principles

### Visual Design
- **Style:** Modern, clean, minimal UI
- **Color Scheme:** Neutral, professional colors with good contrast
- **Responsiveness:** Mobile-first approach (mobile → tablet → desktop)
- **Layout:** Spacious, uncluttered design with clear visual hierarchy

### User Experience
- Clear visual feedback for ALL actions
- Loading, error, and success states for every operation
- Graceful error handling with actionable messages
- Smooth transitions and animations
- Progressive disclosure (show relevant options at the right time)

## shadcn/ui Components

### Component Usage
- Use ONLY shadcn/ui components for UI elements
- Import components from `@/components/ui/`
- Customize using Tailwind classes (no custom CSS unless necessary)
- Follow shadcn/ui composition patterns

## Camera Component Guidelines

### Camera Access Flow
1. Request camera permission
2. Show live preview when granted
3. Display clear error message if denied
4. Offer file upload as fallback

### Camera Best Practices
- Use appropriate resolution constraints
- Clean up media streams when done (stop tracks)
- Handle both desktop and mobile cameras
- Test on various devices

### Layout
- Display presets as a grid of buttons/cards
- Provide custom text input field for advanced users
- Clear visual indication of selected style
- Mobile-responsive grid layout

### Mobile Considerations
- Large touch targets (min 44x44px)
- Thumb-friendly button placement
- Optimized camera UI for mobile
- Landscape and portrait support
